title: $:/plugins/nikorion/base-fields/language/en-GB/history
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''0.1.0'' -- 2026.09.03 -- Hello !
* ''0.2.0'' -- 2026.09.21 -- Add `lifecycle` and `needs`, split `maturity` into `stub` / `rough` / `stable` (`archived` and `deprecated` move to `lifecycle`, the latter renamed `obsolete`), add the `source` role, show `status` on hubs and routines, hide `maturity` and `needs` on register and task roles
* ''0.3.0'' -- 2026.09.26 -- Replace `tools` with the `technology` and `equipment` list fields, add `epistemology` (single value, typed or picked, like `project`) and the `disciplines` list field, add the `project` and `tool` roles, group the `role` values under headings, edit `maturity`, `lifecycle` and `status` with radio buttons, make an empty `maturity` mean `stub` (like an empty `lifecycle` means `active`), show `status` on tasks, task lists and routines or when there is no role, frame in red a field the current role does not use, give each list field a fallback pill colour of its own that follows the palette's light or dark scheme, let `bf-list-pill` render without its remove button (`readonly="yes"`, used by TW-Dynamic-Table's list columns)
* ''0.4.0'' -- 2026.09.28 -- The fields and their vocabularies, icons, labels and translations move to the new [[KMS Ontology|https://github.com/nikorion/TW-KMS-Ontology]] plugin, now required; this plugin keeps the editor. Controls are drawn from each field's definition (`kind`), so a field added to the ontology gets one with nothing to change here; rows and radio controls are configurable (`$:/config/nikorion/base-fields/row/…`, `…/control/…`). Every label shows the field's description as its tooltip; any field that does not apply but holds a value is framed in red. The Vocabularies tab becomes the ontology's //Fields// tab. The `bf-vocab-*` helpers stay as deprecated aliases of `kms-vocab-*`, and icons set by 0.3 keep showing; pill colours move to `$:/config/nikorion/kms-ontology/<field>/Colour`.
